<title>FRANCE: Elf stock steady on Suez sale.</title>
<headline>Elf stock steady on Suez sale.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in energy group Elf Aquitaine Elf Aquitaine were steady after the company announced the widely anticipated sale of its 2.9 percent stake in Compagnie Financiere de Suez.</p>
<p>Elf's stock was 0.12 percent lower at 403.50 francs, while Suez's stock was 0.78 percent higher at 207.40.</p>
<p>Brokers said the transaction was part of Elf's strategy to sell its financial holdings. Since the start of the year, it has sold its stakes in Petrofina, Compagnie Generale des Eaux and Cie Nationale de Portefeuille.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
